# Build-context exclusions for backend/.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CRITICAL — DO NOT ADD `models/` TO THIS FILE.
# backend/models/ is gitignored (serialized ML binaries are not source), but it
# is REQUIRED AT RUNTIME: settings.ML_MODEL_PATH resolves into it, and with
# SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=true the app now refuses to start without a loadable
# artifact. Excluding it produces an image that fails its own startup assertion.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Secrets — credentials are injected at RUN time (compose env_file), never baked
# into a layer. Anything baked in is recoverable from the image forever.
.env
.env.*

# Python bytecode / tooling caches
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Tests: integration tests that talk to a real DB have no business in a
# production image (and conftest now refuses to run against the live DB anyway).
tests/

# Legacy SQLite-era artifacts (the platform is on PostgreSQL since Pre-M7 Step 1)
data/
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Local-only outputs / VCS
output/
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
